# Error Handling

- Expect failure. Fail safely. Prefer recoverable paths.
- Users get helpful messages. Developers get diagnostics.
- Never expose stack traces to end users.
- Data views handle loading, empty, success, error, and permission denied.
- Retry only when safe and idempotent; do not blindly retry inventory/sale mutations.
- Operations should complete or fail cleanly — no partial business updates.
